cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite the paper below.
title: >-
  Restoring the Truncated Band: Geometry-Aware Spectral Operators
  and a Direct Measurement of Geometric Forgetting
authors:
  - family-names: Singh
    given-names: Sehaj R.
version: v1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sehajr-singhs/agfno"
url: "https://sehajr-singhs.github.io/agfno/"
abstract: >-
  Fourier Neural Operators learn solution operators for PDEs, but their only
  global channel - the truncated spectral convolution - is structurally
  band-limited. We show this makes FNOs forget domain geometry as depth grows,
  introduce a zero-gated SDF modulation of the spectral weights that restores
  the truncated band at identical compute, and directly measure geometric
  forgetting via a linear probe on layer activations. The effect replicates
  across seeds, PDE families, and in 3-D (spheres and tori), where depth-16
  FNO collapses (rel-L2 ~ 1.01) while the geometry-aware operator remains
  depth-stable (0.11).
keywords:
  - neural operators
  - Fourier neural operator
  - geometric forgetting
  - scientific machine learning
  - PDEs
